<title>UK: EMU criteria must be taken seriously - Trichet.</title>
<headline>EMU criteria must be taken seriously - Trichet.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of France governor Jean-Claude Trichet said on Wednesday that the convergence criteria for European monetary union (EMU) must be taken very seriously.</p>
<p>&quot;I stress...it is very important we take seriously the question of convergence and therefore the question of criteria,&quot; he said in a speech to the French Chamber of Commerce in London.  </p>
<p>He said that sticking firmly to the EMU criteria would in no way result in a two-speed Europe. &quot;To say that this is a vision of a two-speed Europe is absolutely untrue,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Trichet said that France had a lot of impediments to labour flexibility. &quot;They are a big liability in the present juncture of the French economy,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>He added that Denmark and the Netherlands were good examples of how to successfully combine the same social values as France with rapid job creation.</p>
<p>-- Jennifer Scott +44 171 542 7715</p>
